# Testing Policy: Pytest Fixtures

Prefer pytest fixtures over unittest-style setup methods.

## Rules

- Prefer explicit function-scoped fixtures for test setup.
- Use broader fixture scope only when shared setup is demonstrably safe and materially reduces work.
- Avoid `autouse` fixtures unless the behaviour genuinely applies to every test in scope.

## Rationale

Explicit, narrow fixtures make setup dependencies visible and limit accidental cross-test coupling.
